const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"更多行不一定是更多独立信息",en:"Rows are not independent evidence"},body:{zh:"Petersen研究公司金融与资产定价中常见的面板数据：同一家公司跨年度的残差可能相关，同一年不同公司的残差也可能相关。忽略这些联系，会让不确定性的估计失真。",en:"Petersen studies panels where residuals may correlate within firms over time or across firms in a year. Ignoring these links can distort uncertainty, even with many rows."}},{title:{zh:"分别构造公司效应与时间效应",en:"Separate firm effects from time effects"},body:{zh:"工作论文先模拟同一公司跨期相关，再模拟同一时期跨公司相关，随后把两者组合。Fama–MacBeth与按公司聚类针对的依赖结构不同，因此不能因为两者都常见就互换。比较结果之前，先指出你的数据可能在哪个方向共享误差。",en:"The working paper first simulates within-firm dependence, then within-period dependence across firms, before combining them. Fama–MacBeth and firm-clustered inference address different dependence patterns; their popularity does not make them interchangeable. Identify which observations may share errors before comparing reported significance."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w11280/w11280.pdf",label:{zh:"2006年工作论文引言：第II–IV节的比较设计",en:"2006 working-paper introduction: design of Sections II–IV"}}},{title:{zh:"先描述依赖，再选择标准误",en:"Describe dependence first"},body:{zh:"论文比较文献中常见的处理方法，并解释它们何时一致、何时不同。本站建议先写清观测单位、公司与时间维度、可能共同的冲击，再选择方法，不按哪一种给出的显著性更高来挑选。",en:"The paper compares common approaches and explains when they agree or diverge. Define the observation unit, firm/time dimensions and common shocks before choosing a method, not after comparing significance."}},{title:{zh:"控制平均差异不等于处理全部相关",en:"Mean controls and dependence differ"},body:{zh:"把公司或年度差异放入模型，与正确估计剩余误差的相关结构，是两个相关但不同的任务。固定效应不能被当作自动解决一切标准误问题的标签；具体设定仍要回到原文与数据结构。",en:"Controlling average firm or year differences is distinct from estimating remaining residual dependence. Fixed effects are not a label that automatically resolves every standard-error problem; specifications must match the data structure."}},{title:{zh:"标准误修正不能修复解释变量内生性",en:"An uncertainty correction does not fix endogeneity"},body:{zh:"第II.A节为说明标准误问题，明确假设模型设定正确，解释变量与误差独立。这使讨论聚焦于相关误差带来的不确定性。编辑建议：将这一前提单列；即使聚类方式合适，遗漏变量、反向因果或错误时间对齐仍可能影响系数，不能被一个“稳健”标签消除。",en:"Section II.A assumes a correctly specified model with regressors independent of errors to isolate the uncertainty problem. Editorial application: state that premise separately. Appropriate clustering does not remove coefficient problems arising from omitted variables, reverse causality or incorrect timing; the word 'robust' is not a general identification guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w11280/w11280.pdf",label:{zh:"2006年工作论文第II.A节：模型前提",en:"2006 working paper §II.A: model assumptions"}}},{title:{zh:"把阅读路线落到数据组织",en:"Make the panel structure explicit"},body:{zh:"从事件研究继续到这篇，重点转向多个公司与多个时点的共同变化。本站建议保存稳定实体ID、期间、版本和分组键，检查重复观测；若基础表就把修订当成独立样本，后续统计修正不能恢复正确的信息集合。",en:"Following event studies, focus on common variation across firms and dates. Keep stable IDs, periods, versions and grouping keys; audit duplicates. Statistical corrections cannot repair amendments mistakenly counted as independent observations."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"补充细节来自2006年工作论文，正式发表身份保留。依赖方向、分组数量与模型设定决定适用方法，没有一种标准误对所有数据都正确。",en:"Additional detail comes from the 2006 working paper, separately from its final publication identity. Dependence direction, cluster counts and specification matter; no standard-error method is universally correct."}};export{e as default};
